 "notes": [
  {
   "title": "Region hosting is not sovereignty",
   "text": "US law (including the CLOUD Act) can compel a US-parent company to produce data wherever its servers are. A UK or EU region gives data residency, not jurisdictional control."
  },
  {
   "title": "What actually removes that reach",
   "text": "Keeping inference inside your own boundary: open weights on your own hardware, or a domestic sovereign model. Zero-retention terms and cloud data boundaries reduce exposure but remain a US stack."
  },
  {
   "title": "Where the open-weight frontier sits",
   "text": "Most leading open-weight models now come from Chinese developers. Self-hosting gives control of the model, not of its supply chain."
  }
 ],
